<script>
  import Counter from '../components/Counter.deshi';
</script>

<head>
  <title>Counter · Deshi Islands</title>
  <meta name="description" content="Per-usage island hydration: client:click, client:visible, client:idle." />
</head>

<div class="counter-page">
  <span class="badge">Route: /counter</span>
  <h1>Counter islands</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Opening this route does <strong>not</strong> download <code>Counter.js</code>
    (same as Astro when you skip <code>client:load</code>). You should only see
    the tiny <code>islands.js</code> runtime. Component JS loads when that island
    is needed.
  </p>

  <section class="island">
    <h2>1 · client:click</h2>
    <p>Needed on interaction — Counter.js loads when you press +1.</p>
    <Counter client:click client:props={{ start: 0, step: 1 }} />
  </section>

  <div class="spacer" aria-hidden="true">
    <p>↓ scroll — client:visible loads Counter.js when this block enters the viewport ↓</p>
  </div>

  <section class="island">
    <h2>2 · client:visible</h2>
    <p>Astro client:visible: hydrate on scroll-into-view. No click required.</p>
    <Counter client:visible client:props={{ start: 0, step: 1 }} />
  </section>

  <div class="spacer" aria-hidden="true">
    <p>↓ keep scrolling — client:idle hydrates after this block is on screen and the thread is free ↓</p>
  </div>

  <section class="island">
    <h2>3 · client:idle</h2>
    <p>Hydrate when visible and idle — so visiting /counter does not fetch Counter.js.</p>
    <Counter client:idle client:props={{ start: 0, step: 1 }} />
  </section>
</div>

